# Task 1 Report: Shared C/A Trace Cores With Legacy Parity

## STATUS

DONE

## Files changed

- `core/canslim/earnings_trace.py` (created)
- `core/canslim/c_current_earnings.py`
- `core/canslim/a_annual_earnings.py`
- `.superpowers/sdd/2026-08-26-task11-engine-fidelity-observability/task-1-report.md` (created)

## Implementation summary

- Added the closed `MetricFamily` and `TraceReason` vocabularies and frozen,
  slotted `CTrace` and `ATrace` dataclasses.
- Added the PIT provenance attribute constant and non-mutating ISO-date mapping
  readers. Absent provenance leaves trace public-date fields as `None`; supplied
  malformed provenance or a supplied mapping missing a selected period triggers
  the trace core's broad `EVALUATOR_EXCEPTION` fallback.
- Added `evaluate_c_with_trace` and `evaluate_a_with_trace`, retaining the
  existing metric precedence, matching/annual selection, scoring, clipping,
  weights, and broad exception behavior. Their terminal reasons classify the
  selected value pair without treating below-target finite growth as unavailable.
- Replaced each legacy evaluator body with the required trace-core delegation.

