## Self-review findings

- The legacy public functions consist solely of delegation and tuple projection.
- The core preserves the old row-selection helpers and score calculations, so
  ordinary frames without the optional provenance attribute retain scalar output.
- The selected C trace uses the existing newest-first fiscal matching result;
  selected A dates are the actual two latest non-null, sorted annual columns.
- No test file was created or run, per the task constraint. No network, provider,
  backtest, cache, optimizer, git-write, or other unrelated operation was used.

## Concerns

- None.

## Pre-review correction: strict trace provenance

The trace evaluators now run a single shared evaluator core in strict-provenance
mode. A supplied malformed mapping, or a supplied mapping missing either
selected period, propagates `ValueError` from `evaluate_c_with_trace` or
`evaluate_a_with_trace`. The legacy wrappers use the same core with provenance
disabled, so optional frame attributes cannot affect their scalar tuple.

